if SHIELD_ESB_NAPE_TOUCHTEST

config ESB_NAPE_TOUCHTEST_LANDSCAPE_PATTERN
	bool "Landscape pattern variant (esb_nape_patternls bisect)"
	default n
	help
	  Set by the esb_nape_patternls shield, which drives the panel
	  in the Prospector Scanner's landscape geometry (280x240).
	  The touch test then loads its static test-pattern screen
	  first at boot, laid out compactly for 240 rows (touch
	  navigation is not usable in that geometry). With this off,
	  the touch test behaves exactly as before.

# Touch bring-up test variant layered on esb_nape_disptest: no
# Kconfig changes of its own. Since the Step 2 dedupe, the touch
# devicetree (CST816T on &xiao_i2c / i2c1 at 100 kHz, irq D0 /
# reset D1, PAW3222 + SPI1 disabled, kscan parked on P1.03) and
# the driver's interrupt mode come from the disptest layer
# (esb_nape_disptest.overlay / .conf); this shield's overlay
# defines no nodes. What remains here is the test app (hardware
# I2C scan cross-check + tap / test-pattern screens,
# src/touch_test.c) and the LVGL widget extras in
# esb_nape_touchtest.conf. Keyboard name etc. still come from
# esb_nape_rx.

endif
